WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.830
Redcar, on the Tees estuary
in north-east England.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.330
A steel place.

3
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.110
By 2015, its steelworks belonged
to Sahaviriya Steel Industries,

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.890
a company from Thailand.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.710
In 2015, those steelworks
went into liquidation.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.610
The government called the closure
a huge blow to local people.

7
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.870
The decision was taken by
a foreign-owned company.

8
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.750
So why did a town in England feel it?

9
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.750
In this mission, you'll
map the flows of people,

10
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.030
resources, money and ideas
that tie a place to the world.

11
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.030
Then you'll follow what happened
next, as government stepped in.

12
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: explain why Redcar felt the
closure of a steelworks owned from Thailand.
